        "original_id": "b2ecb032-67cb-54bc-8de8-1e0b5caf8206",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Catuaba\n- Languages: Guarani language, Paraguayan Guarani\n- Peoples: Guarani\n- Places: Brazil, South America\n- Concepts: Tupi–Guarani family, Tupian languages\n\nFacts:\n- Catuaba is used for infusions made from the bark of several tree species native to Brazil.\n- The name Catuaba comes from a Guarani word meaning \"what gives strength to the Indian.\"\n- Guarani is an indigenous language of South America.\n- Paraguayan Guarani is the primary variety of the Guarani language.\n- Paraguayan Guarani has the endonym \"avañe'ẽ,\" meaning \"the people's language.\"\n- The Guarani language belongs to the Tupi–Guarani family within the Tupian languages.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "727ee443-d2a6-50cf-ad8a-792ff314869e",
